{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '2480,2558p' test/yang/clojure_test.clj; sed -n '2500,2590p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj; sed -n '260,310p' src/cljc/yang/correspondence_verifier.clj\"","aggregated_output":"              (into {} (map (fn [op] [op (:yin.k/arities (get data/data-profiles op))]))\n                    (keys portable))))))\n\n\n(def ^:private library-opts\n  {:convention :arg-vector, :outcomes true\n   :adapters yang/library-adapters\n   :native vm/primitive-profiles})\n\n\n(defn run-guest-machine\n  \"Run an AST through either observer composition with a finite instruction\n   budget. Return the terminal machine so fixtures can observe its streams.\"\n  [ast modules lane step-limit]\n  (let [run-bounded (fn [machine]\n                      (loop [v machine, n 0]\n                        (cond\n                          (or (vm/halted? v) (vm/blocked? v)) v\n                          (= n step-limit) (throw (ex-info \"Guest instruction budget exhausted\"\n                                                           {:lane lane :steps n :consumer v}))\n                          :else (recur (vm/step v) (inc n)))))\n        semantic? (= lane :semantic)\n        machine (if semantic?\n                  (semantic/create-vm {:make-stream tu/make-stream\n                                       :capability-secret tu/secret :modules modules})\n                  (tu/create-vm {:modules modules}))\n        session (tu/make-observer-session machine)\n        load-program (if semantic?\n                       (fn [v rows stamp]\n                         (vm/check-contract! vm/ast-contract stamp)\n                         (semantic/load-vector v (:vector (linearize/project-rows rows))\n                                               vm/semantic-contract))\n                       ast-walker/vm-load-program)\n        queued ((if semantic? tu/queue-rows! tu/queue-ast!) session ast)]\n    (-> (observer/run-on-stream queued engine/ready-for-ingress?\n                                (vm/fresh-code-loader load-program vm/ast-contract)\n                                run-bounded)\n        :consumer)))\n\n\n(defn run-guest-machine-depth\n  \"Like run-guest-machine, but records the maximum continuation depth\n   (the semantic lane's K-vector length, or the walker lane's :next chain\n   length) across the run, and returns the terminal machine with the max\n   depth attached under `:max-depth`.\"\n  [ast modules lane step-limit]\n  (let [depth-of (if (= lane :semantic) semantic-depth walker-depth)\n        run-bounded (fn [machine]\n                      (loop [v machine, n 0, mx (depth-of machine)]\n                        (cond\n                          (or (vm/halted? v) (vm/blocked? v)) (assoc v :max-depth mx)\n                          (= n step-limit) (throw (ex-info \"Guest instruction budget exhausted\"\n                                                           {:lane lane :steps n :consumer v}))\n                          :else (let [v' (vm/step v)]\n                                  (recur v' (inc n) (max mx (depth-of v')))))))\n        semantic? (= lane :semantic)\n        machine (if semantic?\n                  (semantic/create-vm {:make-stream tu/make-stream\n                                       :capability-secret tu/secret :modules modules})\n                  (tu/create-vm {:modules modules}))\n        session (tu/make-observer-session machine)\n        load-program (if semantic?\n                       (fn [v rows stamp]\n                         (vm/check-contract! vm/ast-contract stamp)\n                         (semantic/load-vector v (:vector (linearize/project-rows rows))\n                                               vm/semantic-contract))\n                       ast-walker/vm-load-program)\n        queued ((if semantic? tu/queue-rows! tu/queue-ast!) session ast)]\n    (-> (observer/run-on-stream queued engine/ready-for-ingress?\n                                (vm/fresh-code-loader load-program vm/ast-contract)\n                                run-bounded)\n        :consumer)))\n\n\n(defn run-guest-ast\n  \"The value from run-guest-machine; shared by library and oracle fixtures.\"\n  [ast modules lane step-limit]\n  (vm/value (run-guest-machine ast modules lane step-limit)))\n\n   admissions through the token, and projected keys (reconstructed\n   from a single-member envelope, member index always zero) agree\n   with the recorded origin for every ordinal. Both coordinates are\n   recorded WHEN ADMITTING, before compilation, validated by the\n   same origin-shape rules as every source origin\n   (`vm/source-origin`), and retained with the compilation as\n   `:admission-origin` plain data. There is no per-JVM global\n   counter (r3 F2) and no default admission stamping every admission\n   alike (r4 F2): every caller supplies its coordinates explicitly,\n   and replay of one retained compilation reuses its recorded\n   coordinate.\"\n  ([fixture admission-scope admission-ordinal]\n   (kernel-compile fixture admission-scope admission-ordinal false))\n  ([fixture admission-scope admission-ordinal retain-input?]\n   (let [coordinate {:fixture (:id fixture) :scope admission-scope :ordinal admission-ordinal}\n         call (kernel-c-program fixture)\n         forms (kernel-closure call)\n         forms-edn (when retain-input?\n                     (correspondence-text/capture! (assoc coordinate :input :forms) forms))\n         call-edn (when retain-input?\n                    (correspondence-text/capture! (assoc coordinate :input :call) call))\n         source-hash (kernel-canonical-source-hash forms call)\n         admission-origin (vm/source-origin\n                            :program [admission-scope admission-ordinal] 0)\n         program (into (into ['(def gate-execution-trace (stream/make 1000000))]\n                             kernel-site-prelude)\n                       (concat (map kernel-trace-form forms) [call]))\n         program (into (yang/library-for program) program)\n         opts (update arg-vector-opts :native into\n                      (map (fn [[op profile]] [(clojure.core/symbol \"stream\" (name op)) profile])\n                           module/stream-profiles))\n         program-edn (when retain-input?\n                       (correspondence-text/capture! (assoc coordinate :input :program) program))\n         options-edn (when retain-input?\n                       (correspondence-text/capture! (assoc coordinate :input :options) opts))\n         compiled (yang/compile-program program true opts)\n         ;; caller-side site ids at the compiled application expressions,\n         ;; post-macroexpansion (R2), with the mechanically derived site\n         ;; table (R7); every assembled definition is instrumented\n         {stamped :ast sites :sites} (kernel-stamp-sites\n                                       compiled (into #{} (map second) forms))\n         missing (unbound-ast-symbols stamped program)]\n     (if (seq missing)\n       {:status :blocked :phase :admission :blocked-by (vec (sort missing))\n        :owners (into {} (for [s missing]\n                           [s (mapv second (filter #(some #{s} (tree-seq coll? seq %)) program))]))}\n       (cond-> {:status :compiled :ast stamped :forms forms :compiled-ast compiled\n                :admission-origin admission-origin\n                :admission-scope admission-scope\n                :admission-ordinal admission-ordinal\n                :site-table (into {} (map (juxt :site identity)) sites)\n                :site-table-hash source-hash\n                :sites sites\n                :canonical-source-hash source-hash}\n         retain-input?\n         (assoc :reconstruction-input\n                {:fixture fixture :forms forms :call call :program program\n                 :program-edn program-edn :forms-edn forms-edn :call-edn call-edn\n                 :options-edn options-edn :options opts :admission-origin admission-origin}))))))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-compile-in-run\n  \"Compile `fixture` as the next admission of `run`: the run's scope\n   with a distinct ordinal assigned by the run composition.\"\n  ([run fixture] (kernel-compile-in-run run fixture false))\n  ([run fixture retain-input?]\n   (kernel-compile fixture (:scope run) (admission-run-ordinal run) retain-input?)))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-c\n  [compiled lane]\n  (if (= :compiled (:status compiled))\n    (assoc (kernel-attempt\n             #(let [machine (compiler-test/run-guest-machine\n                              (:ast compiled) (oracle-registry yang/kind-module) lane 4000000)\n                    v (vm/value machine)\n                    ref (get-in machine [:store 'gate-execution-trace])\n                    handle (get-in machine [:resources (:id ref)])]\n                (when-not (and (vm/halted? machine) handle)\n                  (throw (ex-info \"Execution trace did not complete\" {:lane lane})))\n                {:status :completed :outcome (evidence-data v) :shape (result-shape (evidence-data v))\n                 :executed-calls (tu/drain handle)}))\n           :lane lane)\n    (assoc compiled :lane lane)))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Depth harness (max live-K per workload)\n;; =============================================================================\n;;\n;; Measurement only: no admission gate and no correctness assertions. Each\n        ids (map first sites)\n        targets (map second sites)]\n    (when (or (not= (count ids) (count (set ids)))\n              (not= (count targets) (count (set targets))))\n      (throw (ex-info \"Ambiguous stamp binding\" {:rule :verifier/binding})))\n    (into {} sites)))\n\n\n(defn attributed?\n  \"Query one already-scoped fixture's table, bindings and complete lane traces.\n   This query does not validate those inputs or authorize reliance on them.\"\n  [{:keys [site-table bindings lanes origin root guest-symbol requested-arity carriers]}]\n  (letfn [(eligible?\n            [entry]\n            (when (and (vector? entry) (= 3 (count entry)))\n              (let [[function arity site] entry\n                    row (get site-table site)\n                    key (get bindings site)]\n                (and row (= site (:site row)) (vector? key) (= 3 (count key))\n                     (vm/occurrence-origin? origin) (= origin (first key))\n                     (jing/segment-address? root) (= root (second key)) (vector? (nth key 2))\n                     (not= :gate-site/none site)\n                     (or (and (= function guest-symbol) (= arity requested-arity))\n                         (some (fn [[carrier carrier-arity mode]]\n                                 (and (contains? #{:ambient-delegation :context-shift :context-copy} mode)\n                                      (= function carrier) (= arity carrier-arity)\n                                      (= carrier (:callee row)) (not (:delegation? row))\n                                      (or (not= :ambient-delegation mode)\n                                          (= :ambient-literal (first (:arg-shapes row))))))\n                               carriers))))))]\n    (every? (fn [lane-id]\n              (let [lane (get lanes lane-id)]\n                (and (= :completed (:status lane)) (true? (:complete? lane))\n                     (some eligible? (:executed-calls lane)))))\n            [:c-walker :c-semantic])))\n\n\n(defn check-fixture!\n  \"Run independent static checks for one supplied compilation. This does not\n   establish admission authenticity, executable-image derivations, trace\n   completeness, durable retrieval, or D1 reliance.\"\n  [{:keys [fixture before stamped origin constructors forms call source-hash\n           site-table bindings metadata]}]\n  (letfn [(require!\n            [condition stage]\n            (when-not condition\n              (throw (ex-info \"Independent fixture check refused\"\n                              {:rule :verifier/fixture :fixture fixture :stage stage}))))]\n    (require! (and fixture (vm/occurrence-origin? origin) (map? before)\n                   (map? stamped) (set? constructors) (some? forms) (some? call)\n                   (string? source-hash) (map? site-table) (map? bindings)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/agents/build-n-test.md | head -85; cat collab/yang-clojure/1794671000001-d1-bounds-declaration-draft.md | head -45'","aggregated_output":"---\ndescription: Build, lint, test commands, TDD guidelines, and bracket debugging for Clojure, ClojureScript, Node.js, and ClojureDart\n---\n\n# BUILD & TEST\n\n## Commands\n\n```sh\n# Tests (Babashka runner)\nbb test              # All three lanes (JVM, Node, Dart), fast default form: no slow tests\nbb test:all          # Every test on every lane, slow ones included (JVM takes 20+ min)\nbb test:slow         # Only the slow tests, on every lane\n# One lane alone: <task>:clj, <task>:cljs, <task>:cljd\nbb test:clj          # JVM, fast: skips ^:slow (bare `clj -M:test` runs them too)\nbb test:cljs         # Node (shadow-cljs :cljs alias), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\nbb test:cljd         # Dart (needs flutter on PATH), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\nbb test:all:clj      # JVM, no filter: `clojure -M:test`\nbb test:all:cljs     # Node with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:all:cljd     # Dart with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:slow:clj     # JVM: `-i :slow` (long-loops-test, ~14 min)\nbb test:slow:cljs    # Node: only the namespaces that use dao.test-slow/guard, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:slow:cljd    # Dart: only those namespaces' generated tests, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\n# Slow tests: tag a deftest ^:slow. The JVM runner then excludes it from `bb test:clj`.\n# Node and Dart have no tag filter, so a .cljc slow test also wraps its body in\n# (dao.test-slow/guard \"name\" (fn [] ...)); it prints SKIP unless DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1.\n# Node and Dart select slow tests by NAMESPACE (derived by grepping `slow/guard`\n# under test/), so the non-slow tests inside those namespaces also run there.\n# On Node, shadow also runs the test namespaces those nine require (about\n# seven more, e.g. lower-portable-test); on Dart only the nine namespaces run.\n# Run test:slow / test:all before a big merge or a commit that touches many parts.\n# Run one Dart lane at a time per machine (the limit is cores and the Flutter cache,\n# not subsystems). On the many-core remote hosts see \"Remote test servers\" below for\n# which lanes may overlap.\n#\n# When to tag a test slow: when it takes more than about 5 s on any lane (the\n# Python e2e tests sit on a ~3 s floor, so their JVM cut is 3.0 s). The\n# default lanes must stay in minutes; 22 JVM tests (0.75% of the suite) were\n# 81% of its test time. Tag it ^:slow on the JVM; if it is a .cljc test, also\n# wrap its body in dao.test-slow/guard so Node and Dart skip it by default. A\n# test that is slow only on Dart (dao.jing.dht-test/unproven-chunks-... takes\n# 72 s there, 3.6 s on the JVM) is a candidate for a speed investigation first.\n# Python slow set (2026-10-06): 65 ^:slow and 15 guard-only tests in the\n# yang.python.antlr e2e, e2e-c1, prelude-parity, safepoint, float-address\n# and int-contract tests; a Python slice landing runs `bb test:sub:clj yang.python --slow`\n# (or `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n <ns>`).\n# While iterating, use the Gate Ladder (see below): G0 iterate via `bb test:sub:clj <own>`\n# or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`. Do not run the full `bb test` while iterating.\n# When a test fails, reproduce and fix it by running ONLY the failing test\n# (`clojure -M:test -n <ns> -v <ns>/<var>`, Node `--test=<ns>`, Dart `--only <ns>`) --\n# never the whole suite (owner ruling 2026-11-01; see Gate Ladder G0).\n# Individual tests run fine on the laptop; suite-scale runs (G1 subsystem sets,\n# G2 changed sets, full suites, slow tier, nightly) run on shiva/jupiter --\n# the suite has outgrown the laptop (owner ruling 2026-11-04).\n# At slice checkpoints, run G1 (`bb test:sub <own>`). Before landing a slice, run\n# G2 (`bb test:changed` in the worktree across all three lanes).\n# Full repo-wide `bb test` runs once daily on the remote hosts (04:00 VN);\n# a MERGE needs only the affected tests (bb test:changed) -- owner ruling 2026-11-01;\n# for a fix branch, the previously-failing tests green IS the merge bar\n# (owner ruling 2026-11-07; see Gate Ladder G0).\n# Cross-host bugs show only on Node or Dart, so tri-host verification is mandatory\n# for every gate from G1 upward. Run one lane set at a time per machine to avoid\n# contention (a laptop has 8 cores; the 24- and 48-core remote hosts have room to\n# overlap lanes, see \"Remote test servers\" below).\n# Measured fast-lane times (2026-10-03): bb test about 14 min = JVM 5.5 + Node\n# 3.8 + Dart 4.3, plus builds. test:slow: Node and Dart about 5 min each (mostly\n# compile); the JVM half is estimated at 17 min (long-loops-test alone is 14),\n# not yet run end to end. test:all: JVM 20+ min, also an estimate.\nnpm test             # Node.js tests\n\n# Cross-host peers the JVM lane spawns. `bb test` builds both. A bare\n# `bb test:clj` builds only the Node REPL (it depends on build:yin-repl-node);\n# without build:yin-repl-peer first, the Dart-peer tests skip with a printed notice.\n# Under `bb test:sub` and `bb test:changed`, prerequisites are derived automatically.\nbb build:yin-repl-peer   # Dart exe build/yin-repl-peer (yin.repl R5 pairs)\nbb build:yin-repl-node   # Node REPL target/yin-repl.js; REQUIRED by\n                         # yin.repl.dht-process-test (JVM-to-Node DHT reader,\n                         # and the linker L5 Node reader that requires a module\n                         # by name): `clojure -M:test` without it fails that test\n```\n\n### Changed-only tests: `bb test:changed`\n\n`bb test:changed` (src/dev/affected.clj) runs the fast tests a change can\nreach: the reverse require closure of the files changed since the\n# D1 bounds declaration — DRAFT (static per-fixture gates; prepares the r9 tagged run)\n\nCreated: 2026-11-14. Role: VM Engineer (compiler provenance), thread\n1794422563000 (D1 correspondence), round r8 deliverable 3.\n\n**Status: DRAFT ONLY — no run has been performed under these ceilings,\nand nothing here authorizes a tagged run or reliance.** This declaration\nis written AFTER the r8 static corpus run (its numbers are that run's\nmeasurements) and BEFORE any r9 tagged verification run, per the partial\nround's requirement that a finite D1 declaration precede any tagged\nrun. The r8 run itself was NOT a ceiling-governed run: it is the\nmeasurement source. The ceilings in section 3 become binding for the\nfirst run declared under them (r9's tagged run), which must re-state\nor tighten them from its own measurements.\n\nThe r8 gates are STATIC: no C lanes were run, no guest fuel consumed, no\ntraces recorded. Lane-quantity ceilings (guest instructions, trace\nrecords and capacity) are therefore NOT declared here; r9 must measure\nand declare them before its run. cc3 v2.1 historical maxima remain\nbaselines only, not D1 numbers.\n\n## 1. Pinned corpus, revision, host, and settings\n\n| Item | Pinned value |\n|---|---|\n| Worktree / branch | /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-d1, branch d1-correspondence @ 56cc5ca3 + the uncommitted r1-r8 diff |\n| Tracked diff (git diff, all of it test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj) | 33,521 B, SHA-256 55c766cb5eef958f26b3ed03cb9169022cb66869fb8734777477fd65cd89dff1 |\n| New untracked code | src/cljc/yang/correspondence_batch.clj; test yang/correspondence_batch_test.clj (all other r1-r7 files unchanged this round) |\n| Corpus (the whole workload) | test/yang/latte_oracle/kernel_gate.edn, SHA-256 8763e273e08259686477315f41956d7005981327b7965bf01e83f9cce487c3e3, 155 fixtures |\n| Frozen v1 evidence | test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_site_tables.edn, SHA-256 e435ac4072ba0a3c278fbe91918d22184b43f0a8d6c1e397c09f68dd629beb75 (unchanged since r1) |\n| Run record | collab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-correspondence-r8.outcomes.edn, SHA-256 7c2f9a6a17bdd144ba67be0326dc4b6ebdb6a83a7297ab08ac82e4ef8aef943a — 155 :pass, 0 :refused, 0 :not-run, with per-fixture admission origin, storage delta, elapsed, row counts, site count, mutation-refusal stage |\n| Upstream oracle | latte-kernel 86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279 (deps.edn :test pin) |\n| Host | macOS 26.6.2 arm64, MacBookPro18,3, 17,179,869,184 B RAM |\n| JVM / Clojure | OpenJDK 17.0.18 (Homebrew, 64-Bit Server VM), Clojure 1.12.4, -Xss64m via the :test alias |\n| Driver | d1-corpus-batch! + test-d1-corpus-static-gates in test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj; per-invocation run config target/d1-corpus-run.edn |\n\n## 2. Workload and retained object set\n\nOne fixture static gate, held one fixture at a time (maximum\nsimultaneously retained fixtures: 1; each holder released before the\nnext):\n\n- the admission: a fresh recorded admission coordinate\n  [:source :program [run-scope ordinal] 0] (distinct ordinal per fixture\n  within a batch run scope; fresh scope per batch invocation);\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
