{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'git status --short --branch; ls -lh target/d1-r9e-retained-store collab/yang-clojure/1794720000000-engineer-d1-r9e*; cat collab/yang-clojure/1794720000000-engineer-d1-r9e-fresh-admissions.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md'","aggregated_output":"## HEAD (no branch)\n?? collab/yang-clojure/1794720000000-engineer-d1-r9e-fresh-admissions.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md\n?? collab/yang-clojure/1794720000000-engineer-d1-r9e.outcomes.edn\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 sto  staff   5.7K Nov 17 04:53 collab/yang-clojure/1794720000000-engineer-d1-r9e-fresh-admissions.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 sto  staff   125K Nov 17 04:45 collab/yang-clojure/1794720000000-engineer-d1-r9e.outcomes.edn\n\ntarget/d1-r9e-retained-store:\ntotal 1442864\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 sto  staff   700M Nov 17 04:45 content.jing\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 sto  staff     0B Nov 17 03:35 lock\n# D1 r9e: fresh laptop admissions — static corpus complete; verification incomplete\n\nWorktree mirror; no commit. This is a static-gate progress checkpoint, not a D1 verification result or authorization for reliance. The outcomes file is `collab/yang-clojure/1794720000000-engineer-d1-r9e.outcomes.edn`; consult it for the current per-fixture state. The scratch store `target/d1-r9e-retained-store` must be retained, not cleaned: the owner decision on durable retention location and ownership is pending. It is uncommitted and is not a published durable service.\n\nThe run uses fresh `fresh-admission-run` scopes and run-local ordinals, not the deleted r8 admissions. Each pass records six addresses and the actual admission coordinate, elapsed time, store growth, row and site counts and its declaration-mutation refusal. The gate captures forms, call, program and options at the input boundary, replays the stored program to the root, compares producer and independent bindings, fetches and validates both row closures, runs `check-fixture!`, and requires the mutated declaration to be refused. These are static checks; the gate's own limitations in r7 still apply.\n\nThe first batch completed 5 passes, and its test ran 1 test / 9 assertions with zero failures or errors. Batch 2 completed another 5; batch 3 completed another 25. Their separate post-close/reopen direct-address checks found 60/60 and 210/210 addresses respectively. That is not a complete post-reopen traversal of every row closure. The retained content log was 172,069,545 bytes at the end of batch 3. Per-batch logs are under `target/d1-r9e-batch-02.log` and `target/d1-r9e-batch-03.log`; `target/d1-r9e-batch.clj` runs the next batch and performs direct address checks after closing and reopening. Batch 4 completed 25 further passes, leaving 60 passes, 0 refusals and 95 not run; after close/reopen all 360 direct addresses were available. Its log is `target/d1-r9e-batch-04.log`, the store measured 493,055,591 bytes, and its sampled process heap peak was 3,677,225,328 bytes. Batch 5 completed 25 more passes; its close/reopen found all 510 direct addresses. Its log is `target/d1-r9e-batch-05.log`, store size 562,134,762 bytes and sampled process heap peak 3,546,214,336 bytes. Batch 6 completed 25 more passes; its close/reopen found all 660 direct addresses. Its log is `target/d1-r9e-batch-06.log`, store size 634,626,686 bytes and sampled process heap peak 3,590,144,896 bytes. Batch 7 completed the remaining 45 passes. The full record is 155 passes, 0 refusals and 0 not run. After close/reopen, all 930 direct addresses were available; its log is `target/d1-r9e-batch-07.log`. The final store is 734,517,424 bytes. This batch sampled 3,599,774,656 bytes of used heap. The first batch did not publish a heap sample. Batch 2 sampled a 1,914,713,024-byte process used-heap peak; batch 3 sampled 2,183,660,952 bytes. The existing sampler reads `Runtime.totalMemory - freeMemory` at 5 ms intervals: it can miss transient peaks, includes unrelated process heap, is not a live-object census and excludes the post-batch reopen and all C-lane execution. These observations are not a complete bounds declaration.\n\nHEAD `ccd3648dc4e1877dfed0e507d6f6c0971115bfc2` was clean at start, detached. Corpus SHA-256 `8763e273e08259686477315f41956d7005981327b7965bf01e83f9cce487c3e3`; frozen v1 evidence SHA-256 `e435ac4072ba0a3c278fbe91918d22184b43f0a8d6c1e397c09f68dd629beb75`. Host Darwin arm64, OpenJDK 21.0.2. No tagged run, complete bounds declaration, correspondence companion or verification result has been produced. In particular, current `run-guest-machine` discards successful step counts, and the evict-oldest ring transport plus ordinary post-halt drain does not prove zero trace loss; these must be addressed and measured before a bounded verification result. The executable recipe/dependency and expansion closure, image/derivation and provenance verification, and retention ownership remain open as described in r9c/r9d. No full oracle suite was run.\n\n## Final static checkpoint\n\nEvery fixture recorded `:site-declarations` for its mutated-table refusal. Maxima from the fresh outcomes: per-fixture store growth 17,903,978 bytes, per-fixture elapsed 56,746 ms, either row closure 12,193 rows, sites 451; total sites 20,805. The largest captured batch heap sample was 3,677,225,328 bytes, with the first batch unmeasured. The heap sampler covers process-wide used heap, including the initial batch store open, but not the subsequent post-close reopen; it can miss sub-5-ms peaks. Fixture elapsed covers the complete combined static gate, not individually timed phases. Aggregate store bytes include deduplication and are not standalone serialized object sizes. No lane instruction, record-count, byte, loss/drain, phase or comparable tagged heap measurements were taken. Consequently no finite complete laptop bounds declaration was finalized, and no tagged verification run was performed. The check after reopening confirms direct addresses, not a second full traversal of all row closures.\n\nThe focused first batch test passed 1 test / 9 assertions; later batches invoked the same gate directly, with explicit reopen address checks, and recorded every outcome. clj-kondo on all four correspondence sources, four correspondence tests and `latte_oracle_test.clj` reported 0 errors and 0 warnings. No code changes or new red-first tests were made this round. The full oracle suite was not run. No companion or verification artifact was fabricated: the complete executable/dependency/expansion closure, image and instruction provenance verification, lane counters and completeness checks, and full bounds remain unfinished. Retention location and owner remain pending; preserve `target/d1-r9e-retained-store` and the outcomes file together.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
