{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"head -80 test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj; sed -n '3060,3155p' test/yang/clojure_test.clj; rg -n 'defn semantic-bytecode->ast|defn fetch-tree\"'!'\"' src/cljc\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.latte-oracle-test\n  \"Pinned upstream LaTTe differential harness, slices 1-9 of the Yang gap\n   program. A executes the original library on Clojure. B executes explicit\n   portability source on Clojure; C compiles it through Yang for the walker\n   and semantic VMs. Slice 9 fails closed on the full kernel corpus. The\n   legacy classifier records historical blockers;\n   the context module additionally checks free-symbol admission before C.\n   Adaptations, operation sequences and scope departures live beside the\n   manifest in yang/latte_oracle/.\"\n  (:require [clojure.java.io :as io]\n            [clojure.java.shell :as shell]\n            [clojure.edn :as edn]\n            [clojure.set :as set]\n            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [clojure.string :as str]\n            [clojure.walk :as walk]\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [yin.repl.store :as file-store]\n            [clojure.tools.reader :as r]\n            [clojure.tools.reader.reader-types :as rt]\n            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n            [yang.correspondence :as correspondence]\n            [yang.correspondence-batch :as correspondence-batch]\n            [yang.correspondence-text :as correspondence-text]\n            [yang.correspondence-verifier :as correspondence-verifier]\n            [yang.clojure-test :as compiler-test]\n            [yang.core.call :as call]\n            [yang.core.uast :as u]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n            [yin.vm.data :as data]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows-support :as rows-support]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.derive :as derive]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.ucf :as ucf]))\n\n\n(def ^:private manifest\n  (edn/read-string (slurp (io/resource \"yang/latte_oracle/manifest.edn\"))))\n\n\n(defn- ns-declaration-aliases\n  \"Alias -> full ns symbol, taken from the file's own (ns ...) declaration —\n   never invented: ::alias/kw must read as :that.real.ns/kw.\"\n  [ns-form]\n  (let [alias-map (atom {})\n        consume-spec (fn [spec]\n                       (when (sequential? spec)\n                         (let [lib (first spec)]\n                           (loop [xs (rest spec)]\n                             (when (seq xs)\n                               (if (= :as (first xs))\n                                 (do (swap! alias-map assoc (second xs) lib)\n                                     (recur (drop 2 xs)))\n                                 (recur (next xs))))))))]\n    (loop [clauses (rest (rest ns-form))]\n      (when (seq clauses)\n        (let [clause (first clauses)]\n          (if (and (seq? clause) (= :require (first clause)))\n            (do (loop [reqs (next clause)]\n                  (let [spec (first reqs)]\n                    (when (and (not (nil? spec)) (not (keyword? spec)))\n                      (consume-spec spec)\n                      (recur (next reqs)))))\n                (recur (next clauses)))\n            (recur (next clauses))))))\n    @alias-map))\n\n\n(defn- read-forms\n  \"Read one latte-kernel source file with reader conditionals resolved for\n   :clj, ::alias/kw keywords resolved against the file's own ns declaration,\n   and ::kw resolved against the file's own namespace — so the C leg compiles\n   the same keyword identities the upstream A leg runs.\"\n        (is (= :yang.call/not-callable (:yang.call/reason payload))\n            \"the adoption's refusal is the escaped payload at this boundary\")\n        (is (some? (get-in payload [:yang.call/data :yang.call/callee]))\n            \"the refusal names the callee in its evidence\"))\n      (doseq [entry [nil false]]\n        (let [[tag payload] (run-library\n                              [(list 'let ['m {:yang.call/entry entry :x 42} 'v '[m]]\n                                     '(m :x))]\n                              library-opts lane 1000000)]\n          (is (= :yin.k/error tag) (str \"a \" (pr-str entry) \" entry is present, not absent\"))\n          (is (= :yang.call/not-callable (:yang.call/reason payload))\n              (str \"a \" (pr-str entry) \" entry reaches admission and refuses\"))))\n      (let [[tag payload] (run-library\n                            '[(defn tail-refusal\n                                []\n                                (let [five 5 v [five]] (five 1)))\n                              (tail-refusal)]\n                            library-opts lane 1000000)]\n        (is (= :yin.k/error tag))\n        (is (= {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/not-callable\n                :yang.call/data {:yang.call/callee 5}}\n               payload)\n            \"the refusal survives a tail-position value call as the payload\")\n        (is (= {:yang.call/callee 5}\n               (get-in payload [:yang.call/data]))\n            \"the callee evidence names the scalar callee\"))\n      (doseq [[where form] [[1 '(five (boom) 2)] [2 '(five 1 (boom))]]]\n        (let [[tag payload] (run-library\n                              ['(defn boom\n                                  []\n                                  (throw (ex-info \"boom\" {})))\n                               (list 'let '[five 5 v [five]] form)]\n                              library-opts lane 1000000)]\n          (is (= :yin.k/error tag) (str \"operand \" where \" errors before the refusal\"))\n          (is (= \"boom\" (:yin.k/message payload))\n              (str \"operand \" where \" is evaluated before the callee check\")))))))\n\n\n(deftest test-run-guest-machine-budget-exhaustion-carries-advanced-consumer\n  (let [ast (yang/compile-program\n              '[(def progressed 42)\n                (loop [i 0]\n                  (if (< i 20)\n                    (recur (+ i 1))\n                    (+ progressed i)))])]\n    (doseq [lane [:walker :semantic]]\n      (let [full-steps (loop [m (if (= lane :semantic)\n                                  (let [vm0 (semantic/create-vm {:make-stream tu/make-stream\n                                                                 :capability-secret tu/secret\n                                                                 :modules library-modules})\n                                        sess (tu/queue-rows! (tu/make-observer-session vm0) ast)]\n                                    (:consumer\n                                      (observer/run-on-stream\n                                        sess engine/ready-for-ingress?\n                                        (vm/fresh-code-loader\n                                          (fn [v rows stamp]\n                                            (vm/check-contract! vm/ast-contract stamp)\n                                            (semantic/load-vector v (:vector (linearize/project-rows rows))\n                                                                  vm/semantic-contract))\n                                          vm/ast-contract)\n                                        identity)))\n                                  (let [vm0 (tu/create-vm {:modules library-modules})\n                                        sess (tu/queue-ast! (tu/make-observer-session vm0) ast)]\n                                    (:consumer\n                                      (observer/run-on-stream\n                                        sess engine/ready-for-ingress?\n                                        (vm/fresh-code-loader ast-walker/vm-load-program vm/ast-contract)\n                                        identity))))\n                              n 0]\n                         (when (zero? n)\n                           (is (nil? (get (:store m) 'progressed))\n                               (str lane \": pre-run loaded VM has not executed def yet\")))\n                         (if (vm/halted? m)\n                           n\n                           (recur (vm/step m) (inc n))))\n            budget 25\n            caught (try\n                     (run-guest-machine ast library-modules lane budget)\n                     nil\n                     (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e e))\n            data (ex-data caught)\n            carried (:consumer data)]\n        (is (some? caught) (str lane \": budget exhaustion throws\"))\n        (is (< budget full-steps) (str lane \": chosen budget stops mid-execution\"))\n        (is (= {:lane lane :steps budget} (select-keys data [:lane :steps])))\n        (is (some? carried) (str lane \": ex-data carries :consumer\"))\n        (is (= carried (get-in data [:session :consumer]))\n            (str lane \": observer session carries the same advanced consumer\"))\n        (is (not (vm/halted? carried)) (str lane \": carried consumer is mid-flight\"))\n        (is (= 42 (get (:store carried) 'progressed))\n            (str lane \": carried consumer reflects executed store writes, not step-0 VM\"))\n        (let [[terminal rem-steps] (loop [m carried, k 0]\n                                     (if (vm/halted? m)\n                                       [m k]\n                                       (recur (vm/step m) (inc k))))]\n          (is (= 62 (vm/value terminal)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1497:(defn semantic-bytecode->ast\nsrc/cljc/yang/correspondence_verifier.clj:341:(defn fetch-tree!\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
