urce on lift is specified\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:29:with its owner (§6.3), E2 requires lexical presence and X1 validates the\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:32:cross-lane re-emission takes an explicit stream correspondence (§5.5),\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:36:`bafdec74`), so that §§2.5-2.6, 5.2, 6.1, 6.3, 7, 8.2 state what\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:49:that §§4.1-4.3, 5.2, 5.3, 5.5, 5.6, 6.3, 7, 8.3, 8.5, 9 state what\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:59:(deviations 1-8, design defects D1-D5), the codex review\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:61:D1-D5) and the Architect's rulings\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:146:A continuation is a value: one **canonical frame** of the register machine, which is a `run` state `⟨A, pc, W↾L(pc), E, K⟩` at any instruction boundary (§1.3) or one of its two delivery states, `act` or `tail`, with the saved window, the delivery record and the pending wait the evaluator mints when it parks (frozen §2.4, §4.2); and a task is the product of its activation, its ordered waits and its ordered completed wakes (§2.6); plus the task context it needs: the task's **free\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:176:**DECIDED** (frozen §2.4 \"Delivery\", §4.2; evaluator design §1.3-1.6;\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:212:  (`debruijn/stack.cljc:82, 418, 683`; `debruijn/register.cljc:50`).\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:216:**DECIDED** (frozen §4.2), restated with one naming decision (§10.1 F1):\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:257:The two delivery states of §1.1 are the states at which the evaluator parks by itself. They are special cases of its general state between any two instructions, `⟨A, pc, W↾L(pc), E, K⟩`, which `vm-hot` materializes whenever fuel runs out (`semantic.cljc:142-143`) and which the carrier expresses as the `run` state of §1.2. A step is atomic: effects are observed only inside a step or inside the scheduler's sweep, so no state between steps holds a half-issued effect; atomicity of a step is not transactionality of the outside world (an append performed before a host exception is not undone). A task is a **product**: at most one active activation (the `run`), its ordered pending waits, its ordered completed wakes (the ready queue: a woken wait with the value, status and cursor update its effect produced, carried by the `:ready` row of §2.3), its parked table, and its stores. The scheduler constructs every combination: resuming one of several woken waits leaves the others queued and the unresolved ones pending (`engine.cljc:2294-2312`, `:2305`). Every such state is **representable**. The lift refuses only what is not **portable** (a value with no wire form), not **satisfied** (code or dependencies the receiver lacks), or a **hold** (a driver-internal observation in flight: §7.1 step 1), never a pc. The static correspondence of §4 holds at every pc of a body: distinct virtuals in `L(p) ∪ def(p)` hold distinct physical registers (`derive/allocation`), and the stack kernel's operand region at A pc `p` is `stack-layout(p) ++ uses(p)` above a dead prefix (§4.3); both are checks (§5.6), not theorems. A root whose task has an active activation has kind `:running` (§2.6) and is a custody subject like a blocked or parked root (§7.3).\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:308:**DECIDED** by frozen §4.2's last paragraph; **PROPOSED** names `:act`\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:423:   free-env-cref    ; NEW: a :bindings row, the task's initial free environment (§6.3)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:480:**DECIDED** (frozen §4.2: membership recomputed from A; representation,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:698:image ids), `space`, `segment-of`, `register-pairs`, `correspondence`,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:708:dispatch in one place; the algorithms of §4.2-4.3 are unchanged.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:745:   (`image-row`/`absolute-pc`, `debruijn/register.cljc:326-337`); R's pcs\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:862:1. **pc correspondence.** The stack emitter visits parse nodes in\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1032:names through the task-wide `free-env` (`stack.cljc:683`:\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1068:carried explicitly** (root slot `free-env`, §2.6; §6.3), every `E` is\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1101:§6.3), never reads a native image's hash as an identity, and never\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1144:2. **Closures and continuations in the free environment** (§6.3, R3):\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1148:3. **Primitives in the register kernel's payload** (§4.2, D4): the\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1326:`:591-603`); `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` (a register kernel stepped one\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1435:takes an **explicit logical-stream correspondence** from the fixture:\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1457:`canonical-under` may erase (codex D1, accepted verbatim by R4;\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1461:explicit, injective logical-stream correspondence and a\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1466:the same correspondence before comparison; replacing a whole descriptor\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1484:`stream/descriptor` under the same correspondence and\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1510:   `live` of phase-5 §6.3 row 2.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1540:**Order per point** (reference lane, 6d-a; backends, 6e): at boundary `S_i` of the stepping source: (1) **lift**; (2) **lower** into a fresh receiver of an **isolated world** (§ below); (3) **immediate relift** of the receiver and **law 2** (`canonical-under` root equality with the lift; no execution in between); (4) **law 6** on every lifted frame (plus the two window tampers); (5) **run the receiver to the end** in its world, **law 1** (result and effect trace equal the reference's, after `normalize`'s fresh-identity correspondence); (6) negative controls kept: cursor positions and descriptors, windows and lexical values tampered are refused or differ as today.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1542:**Isolated worlds**: each point builds the receiver's composition and streams fresh from the case's **deterministic script** (the same scripted inputs the reference run saw, fed to the receiver's own streams); the stepping source's world is never shared with a receiver; fresh identities normalise through the existing correspondence (`normalize`, `:238`). The reference result and trace are computed once per case on a pristine world.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1602:### 6.3 The free environment: carrier, source, ownership\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1712:`:free-env` argument, §6.3, never from a current `E`), the result,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1728:continuation in its `:free-env` (§6.3); then, under a lift context\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1739:`:register-layout` of `virt` (§4.2), `:stack-layout`, `:stack-base`,\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794630000000-engineer-attribution-as-query.glm-5.3.stdout.log\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794170000000-architect-cc1-recheck-signed-ruling.findings.md\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794610000000-architect-attribution-as-query-ruling.qwen-review.md\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794600000000-architect-attribution-as-query-ruling.astra-review.stdout.log\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794163259000-architect-cc1-recheck-signed-ruling.findings.md\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793880000000-architect-h3-1-budget-ruling.kimi-k3.1-pro.stdout.log\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795050000000-architect-attribution-as-query-fix-review.diff\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794320000000-architect-cell-ref-two-api-ruling.prompt.md\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794630000000-engineer-attribution-as-query.glm-5.3.r