{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^##? |4'\"\\\\.2|6\\\\.3|dependency|expansion|bounded' collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md | head -80\"","aggregated_output":"1:# Call-site provenance: occurrence contract and durable correspondence\n10:## 1. Decision and evidence limits\n28:## 2. Occurrence contract C1\n38:- `origin` identifies the actual admission or generation event. Admitted syntax uses `[:source medium batch-token j]`; generated syntax uses `[:expansion expansion-record-address]`. Generated post-expansion trees must not be mislabeled as original source or given a fabricated expansion address. If a no-op expansion retains an admitted tree, the original source origin remains valid; “post-expansion” names the pipeline boundary, not proof that a generating event occurred.\n39:- An origin is supplied by the admitting/generating composition. Two separately admitted identical sources have different origins; two identical applications in one tree have different paths; two expansion attempts with identical output have different producing records. Replaying a single recorded admission is different from admitting the same text again.\n41:The implemented origin validator accepts exactly the source and expansion shapes (`src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:938-958`). `vm/occurrences` returns `[root path node-id]`, one per place, with origin fixed by the composition; it does not return full keys or count only distinct row ids (`vm.cljc:1589-1609`).\n65:Finalize paths only after macro expansion, generated-name canonicalization, wrappers, module/SCC assembly, and tail marking that determine the named tree. Source-level annotations alone cannot cover generated calls (base ruling R2 at line 17). Low-level functions returning fragments may defer finalization until an owning root and origin exist; each executable/publication ingress must invoke the common finalizer. A frontend cannot claim adoption by marking just its parser or user-call lowering arm.\n69:Macro expansion already records input root, call path, macro root, parent, output and attempt (`src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:997-1000,1062-1119`). However, final tail marking and stand-in lowering happen later (`:1255-1260`). The implementation inventory must resolve how final published roots are related to these expansion outputs. Whether the existing event/record adapters already provide the complete final-root correspondence is **unknown — the implementation round's inventory decides**. Do not assume an intermediate output record identifies every occurrence in the final assembled tree, and do not mint a fake `:expand` merely to satisfy the shape.\n93:This is a precise proposed spelling for the still-unfrozen oracle implementation. It is **not** a third legal persisted occurrence origin: `vm/occurrence-origin?` must continue rejecting it. An EDN evidence file may preserve an ephemeral id as evidence of that run; that does not convert it into a portable code occurrence. Persisted C1 side tables and expansion links require real ruled origins.\n103:## 3. A2 inventory: revisions, preservation, and refusal\n130:| Surface and inspected locations | Required implementation work / read-only dependency |\n132:| Clojure `compile-form`, `compile`, `compile-program`, `lower-unit`: `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2021,2164,2839,2993` | Cover native and argument-vector/outcome compilation, library/adapters, linked unit wrapping and global publication. Finalize at executable roots, after expansion. Existing fragment APIs need not invent origins. |\n141:| Macro pipeline: `yin/vm/macro.cljc:997-1005,1062-1119,1196-1261` | Keep expansion attempt provenance, resolve final-root ownership, annotate generated occurrences and retain retrievable expansion records. Post-expansion is a required integration point. |\n157:“Side tables are additive” is the compatibility policy, not permission to skip republishing coverage evidence. **Unannotated persisted artifacts remain loadable under their supported existing code contracts.** A provenance-requiring query returns missing provenance/refuses credit; it never invents identity from names, hashes, arities, values or source lines. Old provenance may be reconstructed only when the actual admission/expansion inputs are retained, and the result is a newly verified artifact.\n162:2. For each host publication: canonical row closure, semantic vector, stack/register stored images and checksums, derivation records, schema-1 manifest, pinned dependency addresses, new C1 side tables/provenance/correspondence, and discovery/index/name/signature records where used. The actual publication sequence is `yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:156-209`. Side-only annotation should leave old code addresses unchanged; measure this rather than assume it. New side objects still need publication, retrieval and retention.\n165:5. Oracle evidence: new versioned caller-site tables; `slice9_evidence.edn`, `slice9_verification.edn`, `slice9_declarations.edn`, `slice9_unexercised.edn`, `fixture_closure.edn`, gate markdown and captured verification/test outputs; `context.edn`, `kernel_gate.edn`, `manifest.edn` and earlier slice evidence as input/history or regeneration targets according to actual dependency. Every changed trace-bearing field/pin must be listed; blanket rewriting of historical evidence is not required.\n176:## 4. R1 durable correspondence schema D1\n217:The recipe profile pins frontend/compiler revision, grammar/options, expansion environment and recorded origins/attempts, all code-producing transformations, source canonicalization, site-table derivation, and lowering/provenance rules. The consumer must implement that exact recipe/profile. A missing upstream canonicalization rule is not repaired by choosing a plausible hash. The exact oracle schema identity remains the dependency in §1.1.\n219:`origin-bindings` is an added relation binding evidence-local sites to actual durable occurrences; **it is not a replacement attribution table**. It preserves the oracle's ephemeral ids literally. Validate every endpoint, reconstructed tree and path. A site's mapping must be unique within the claimed compilation. Multiple replay records can name the same durable occurrence only where they explicitly replay the same admission; distinct admissions must remain distinct. An oracle run without durable expansion/source records cannot be promoted merely by changing `:ephemeral` to `:expansion`. It may remain useful oracle evidence without a durable binding. To accept a relying consumer, reproduce the actual compilation under recorded durable admissions/expansions and verify its correspondence; do not retroactively assert an unrecorded event.\n221:### 4.2 Independent reconstruction and discovery\n229:3. Reconstruct the source/adaptation compilation under the exact recipe, using recorded source admissions and expansion attempts; recompute final roots and eligible occurrence sets. Recompute the oracle's canonical-source-hash using its exact rule.\n239:## 5. A3 adoption briefs and ordering\n258:On each host run static occurrence/provenance checks for AST, semantic, stack and register artifacts where the existing format admits the fixture. Execute direct walker and all three vector paths for the portable correctness corpus. Linked paths exercise all supported linked formats and pin existing unsupported/refusal cases explicitly. For example, the inspected TS linked harness documents a walker `:undeclared-free` limitation while using three vector VMs (`test/yang/typescript/antlr/linked_harness.cljc:11-15`); this design does not silently promise that old unrelated limitation is fixed. If a missing lane prevents the required new provenance test, report adoption incomplete with the named dependency.\n262:Build a portable replay fixture containing the SAME source or source-derived CST, grammar/options, compiler/profile revision, canonical naming inputs, source-medium/batch/member coordinates, and expansion environment/attempt inputs. The source origin contract explicitly makes these coordinates supplied plain data (`code-as-tuples.md:405-437`; `vm.cljc:938-958`).\n268:- For expansion fixtures, identical expansion-record addresses under replayed identities and identical producing-record chains. Normalize neither origin nor generated names away after the fact.\n276:**Clojure.** Inventory native/argument-vector/outcome compile options, `compile` vs `compile-program`, `compile-form` callers, macro expansion, `lower-unit`, `library-for`, direct walker/datoms/rows lanes, REPL single/multi-form and linked runtime publication. Show a non-oracle production fixture traversing the full pipeline, including macro-generated and helper calls. Republish `clj` and `yang.call` on each host. Oracle-specific stamping is instantiation #1 only; it does not close this brief. Anchors: `yang/clojure.cljc:2021-2034,2164-2200,2791,2839-2862,2993-3021`.\n286:## 6. Measurement and declared budgets\n314:### 6.3 Bounds published before any tagged run\n320:| Maximum input rows, occurrences, A, D and total path bytes | Derive from the pinned static corpus; reject over-bound traversal before instrumentation. Include generated/bundled prelude expansion, not only source calls. |\n324:| Compile/expand/publish/verify/load/query time | Declare finite absolute time limits and allowed deltas against B/S in the preflight record. Pilot B/S measurements may set these; a tagged timeout is a failed bounded run. |\n335:| Clojure | Native and argument-vector/outcome roots, macro outputs, guest library, linked `clj/yang.call`, repeated REPL admissions; `A_clj + L_clj + sum(P_f)` plus retained expansion/input closure | Nested/multi-arity/indirect/helper/tail calls in both production and oracle-specific fixtures; oracle owns its existing ceilings |\n340:The storage/work formulas are the design's budget impact; numbers require the pinned post-sweep corpus and are not asserted here. Shared `yang.call` must be reported once as retained shared content and separately as each frontend's dependency, avoiding both double charging and disappearance. Prelude republishing on four hosts is mandatory even when code hashes remain unchanged: the new occurrence/provenance artifacts need independent production/load evidence.\n342:## 7. Correctness and refusal gates\n348:| Duplicate content / admission | Two identical applications at different paths; identical roots at two batch indices; identical source admitted twice; identical expansion outputs from two attempts. Distinct K where required, shared content allowed. Tamper one origin/root/path and refuse cross-borrowed evidence. |\n349:| Macro generation | A call introduced only by expansion, nested expansions, repeated expansion attempts, final tail/stand-in transformations, and unexpanded source retained in the same compilation. Reconstruct real producing records; raw-source site counts cannot pass. |\n359:| Stale table and schema | A declared id never observed in a trace produces the recorded diagnostic; unsupported versions, fabricated expansions, extra/conflicting/incomplete marker rows, missing retained inputs and wrong profiles produce distinct failures. Do not silently treat malformed evidence as an honest unexecuted site. |\n361:| Trace completeness | Buffer exhaustion, loss, interrupted run, missing trace lane or partial drains never become positive attribution. Trace-writing infrastructure must not recursively instrument its own bookkeeping into an unbounded trace. |\n365:## 8. Acceptance sequence and owner risks\n367:The design deliverable selects C1 and D1, enumerates the known integration surfaces, and gives each frontend a bounded adoption brief. Implementation remains outside this round.\n372:2. After the cell-ref sweeps/J2 land, refresh the exact producer, validator, artifact and host inventory; identify every changed contract, every read-only dependency, and any required format revision. Resolve final expansion-root ownership and native provenance completeness.\n375:5. Accept each production frontend only after its complete four-host brief, cross-host equality, measurements and correctness/refusal battery pass. Preserve any unsupported lane or withdrawn witness as a failure/dependency, not an unreported skip.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > target/d1-r9f-measure.clj <<'EOF'\n(require '[yang.correspondence-measure :as measure]\n         '[yang.correspondence-batch :as batch]\n         '[yang.latte-oracle-test :as oracle]\n         '[yang.clojure :as yang]\n         '[yin.repl.store :as store])\n(let [source \\\"collab/yang-clojure/1794720000000-engineer-d1-r9e.outcomes.edn\\\"\n      out \\\"collab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-r9f-measurements.edn\\\"\n      dir \\\"target/d1-r9e-retained-store\\\"\n      corpus @(ns-resolve 'yang.latte-oracle-test 'kernel-gate-corpus)\n      ids (mapv :id (:fixtures corpus))\n      old (batch/read-progress source)\n      _ (when-not (= (set ids) (set (keys (:outcomes old))))\n          (throw (ex-info \\\"Corpus disagreement\\\" {:stage :corpus})))\n      _ (when-not (.exists (java.io.File. out)) (measure/initialize\"'! out ids))\n      pending (filter #(= :not-run (get-in (measure/read-progress out) [:outcomes % :status])) ids)\n      todo (take (Long/parseLong (or (first *command-line-args*) \"1\")) pending)\n      sampler ((ns-resolve '\"'yang.latte-oracle-test 'd1-heap-sampler\"'!) 5)\n      h (store/open {:type :file :dir dir})\n      registry ((ns-resolve '\"'yang.latte-oracle-test 'oracle-registry) yang/kind-module)]\n  (try\n    (doseq [id todo]\n      (let [result (try (measure/measure-fixture\"'! h id (get-in old [:outcomes id]) registry 4000000)\n                        (catch Exception e {:status :refused :stage (or (:stage (ex-data e)) :harness)\n                                            :detail (dissoc (ex-data e) :consumer :session)\n                                            :message (ex-message e)}))]\n        (measure/record! out id result)\n        (prn {:fixture id :measurement result}) (flush)))\n    (finally (store/close! h)\n             (prn {:sampled-process-heap-bytes ((:stop! sampler))}) (flush))))\n(shutdown-agents)\nEOF\nset -o pipefail\njava -Xss64m -cp \"$(cat target/d1-r9e-classpath.txt)\" clojure.main target/d1-r9f-measure.clj 1 2>&1 | tee target/d1-r9f-measure-01.log'","aggregated_output":"Loading initial Timbre config from: :default\nWARNING: load already refers to: #'clojure.core/load in namespace: yin.vm.encoder, being replaced by: #'yin.vm.encoder/load\n{:fixture :minimal-last, :measurement {:status :pass, :admission-origin [:source :program [\"d1-r8-corpus-313b026f-bd01-4362-b885-e12f9fa6f757\" 0] 0], :addresses {:evidence :segment/blake3-e4094211c705022e962908b6176cb26b1dca6112af4345addc7acf56b21baee1, :input :segment/blake3-ac696f04cf12957ff0276c8f91c242a1bde65d3a602ccbfa1177733a731c28f4, :profile :segment/blake3-ab1263e1c5b304bda2d1875f4fa78a7a91ca82d4c9435dffa262288e7a9863b0, :snapshot :segment/blake3-755b6da0b4b4aec3457b0ac340a3f3b08db002e42c1812017b70cd011a94e78f, :root :segment/blake3-e92719a0c071f85033ea946b40cce7a8eff643b8c96116f26f75c6e96dc59b2d, :stamped-root :segment/blake3-f3bc79f03c0e152525e4f87c0666a892c579ae2b6817c48043cb92c0ee26e074}, :rows {:pre-stamp 1165, :stamped 1168}, :fetch-ms 173, :lanes {:walker {:record-count 1, :serialized-bytes 22, :lost 0, :drain-outcome :dao.stream/blocked, :steps 4283, :run-ms 154, :drain-ms 2}, :semantic {:record-count 1, :serialized-bytes 22, :lost 0, :drain-outcome :dao.stream/blocked, :steps 2441, :run-ms 278, :drain-ms 0}}, :elapsed-ms 609}}\n{:sampled-process-heap-bytes 3352883456}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
