{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > collab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-r9f-tagged-run.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md <<'EOF'\n# D1 r9f — partial lane instrumentation; sequencing decision pending\n\nWorktree mirror only; no commit. **No complete bounds declaration, tagged verification result, or companion was produced.** The r9e retained store at \"'`target/d1-r9e-retained-store` and its 155-outcome record remain the inputs; retention location and ownership remain an owner decision. The frozen v1 evidence SHA-256 is `e435ac4072ba0a3c278fbe91918d22184b43f0a8d6c1e397c09f68dd629beb75`.\n\n## Sequencing defect and decision\n\nDesign `1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md` §6.3 states bounds must be published **before any tagged run**, while the r9f dispatch asks for retained-corpus C-lane trace measurements before the declaration and then a separate tagged verification under it. The earlier r9e dispatch also explicitly says no tagged run before the declaration. I initially treated measurement execution as distinct from a tagged verification run and executed the retained stamped `:minimal-last` tree on both lanes **before a complete declaration**. That execution did not follow §6.3'\"'s sequencing. It is an unbounded-preflight observation with a 4,000,000 step cap, not a passed bounded run, and it must not be represented as verification or a compliant bounds-governed sample. Once I noticed §6.3's broader wording, I stopped the next process while it was opening the store; it recorded no fixture. Whether the requested measurement is an explicit exception or bounds must come first needs clarification. The retained measurement file explicitly records \"'`:pre-declaration-tagged-execution true`.\n\n## Implemented and observed\n\nWithin the authorized correspondence test surfaces, `test/yang/correspondence_lane.clj` provides a measurement composition with an aggregate counter over actual `vm/step` calls, explicit finite step-budget refusal, and ring-buffer trace draining. It rejects an evicted prefix by checking the ring'\"'s oldest cursor position and requires the full range to drain to its captured tail. This assumes a halted, non-concurrently-written ring trace. Trace bytes are UTF-8 \"'`pr-str` bytes for the vector; they are not buffer occupancy or canonical Jing bytes. `test/yang/correspondence_measure.clj` checks retained fixture/admission/root coordinates, fetches both row closures and measures each lane and its trace. It records per-fixture measurement outcomes atomically and refuses rewrites, but is not a D1 verifier or a declaration enforcer. The driver is `target/d1-r9f-measure.clj`; it must not be resumed until the sequencing decision is resolved.\n\nThe pre-declaration pilot fetched both stored row closures after opening the store and produced walker 4,283 steps / 1 record / 22 printed UTF-8 bytes / 154 ms, semantic 2,441 steps / 1 record / 22 bytes / 278 ms; both ring traces reported zero evicted positions and drained to the captured tail. Fetch was 173 ms; total 609 ms. Process used heap sampled every 5 ms peaked at 3,352,883,456 bytes including store open, not a live-object census; it can miss short peaks. Raw pilot output is `target/d1-r9f-measure-01.log`, and the worktree progress record is `1794422563000-engineer-d1-r9f-measurements.edn`: one measurement pass and 154 not run. The aborted next invocation is `target/d1-r9f-measure-02.log` and has no final heap sample. These timings are single observations and the step ceiling was a safety cap, not a predeclared D1 bound.\n\n## Validation and remaining work\n\nRed first: the lane and progress tests each failed on their missing namespace before implementation. The two focused namespaces pass 3 tests / 18 assertions, including both backends, exact budget refusal, trace prefix eviction and progress finality. clj-kondo reported 0 errors and 0 warnings on the four new correspondence files before the final metadata-only change; rerun after any further edits. Full oracle suite not run.\n\nThe 154 remaining lane measurements have not been made. No complete finite laptop declaration, per-phase baseline/delta experiment, tagged verification under it, corpus-wide second row-closure traversal, executable dependency/expansion recipe closure, image/derivation and instruction-provenance verification, D1 record, companion or separate verification publication exists. The independent `attributed?` function assumes already-complete scoped traces; the new measurement helper does not fill all seven design §4.2 steps. Do not fabricate these artifacts or treat a static or pilot pass as relying-consumer acceptance.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
